        { "id": "c", "text": "$a = 1$, $b = -3$, $c = -10$" },
        { "id": "d", "text": "$a = 3$, $b = 1$, $c = -10$" }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "b",
      "explanation": "Comparing $x^2 + 3x - 10$ with $ax^2 + bx + c$: $a = 1$ (coefficient of $x^2$), $b = 3$ (coefficient of $x$), $c = -10$ (constant term)."
    },
    {
